msgid "Max text item size"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:119
msgid "Maximum size of a text item. Anything out of this boundary is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:127
msgid "Min text item size"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:128
msgid "Minimum size of a text item. Anything out of this boundary is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:135
msgid "The keyboard shortcut to delete the first element in history"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:136
msgid ""
"By default, hitting ctrl + alt + v does that (\"<Ctrl><Alt>V\"). An empty "
"string here disables this functionnality."
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:144
msgid "Does the primary selection affects history?"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:145
msgid "By default, only clipboard (ctrl+c) affects history."
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:152
msgid ""
"Do we save all versions of selected rich text (e.g. html) or just the plain "
"text version?"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:153
msgid "By default, we're saving all"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:160
msgid "The keyboard shortcut to display the menu"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:161
msgid ""
"By default, hitting ctrl + alt + h displays the menu (\"<Ctrl><Alt>H\"). An "
"empty string here disables this functionnality."
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:169
msgid "Where the history is stored"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:170
msgid ""
"The storage backend used to persist the history: \"file\" keeps the current "
"on-disk history, \"sqlite\" stores it in a per-history database (with an "
"\"encrypted-sqlite\" flavor), \"none\" stores nothing. The migration dialog "
"lets the user pick."
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:177
msgid "Last processed storage backend revision"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:178
msgid ""
"Internal: the storage-backend revision the daemon last migrated to. When it "
"differs from the daemon's current revision, the storage migration dialog is "
"shown on startup."
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:185
msgid "The keyboard shortcut to sync the clipboard to the primary selection"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:186
msgid ""
"By default, hitting ctrl + alt + o syncs them (\"<Ctrl><Alt>P\"). An empty "
"string here disables this functionnality."
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:194
msgid "The keyboard shortcut to sync the primary selection to the clipboard"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:195
msgid ""
"By default, hitting ctrl + alt + p syncs them (\"<Ctrl><Alt>P\"). An empty "
"string here disables this functionnality."
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:203
msgid "Are the primary selection and the clipboard synchronized?"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:204
msgid "By default, the primary selection and the clipboard are independent."
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:211
msgid "Do we track the clipboard changes?"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:212
msgid "By default, we're tracking those changes."
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:219
msgid ""
"Do we sync the daemon state with the gnome-shell extension's one? (disable "
"the daemon when disabling the extension)"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:220
msgid "By default, the daemon state keeps unchanged"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:227
msgid "Do we trim the textual items before adding them to history?"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:228
msgid ""
"Trimming means removing all trailing and ending spaces. By default, we're "
"letting them as-is."
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:236
msgid ""
"The keyboard shortcut to upload the first element in history to a pastebin "
"service"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:237
msgid ""
"By default, hitting ctrl + alt + u does that (\"<Ctrl><Alt>U\"). An empty "
"string here disables this functionnality."
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:245
msgid "Do we prompt for confirmation when emptying a history?"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:246
msgid "By default, we do as it's a destructive action"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:253
msgid ""
"Do we run the experimental in-shell (mutter) daemon from the gnome-shell "
"extension?"
msgstr ""

#: data/gsettings/org.gnome.GPaste.gschema.xml:254
msgid ""
"When disabled, the gnome-shell extension is a pure client and the standalone "
"daemon is used instead"
msgstr ""

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:9
msgid "Marc-Antoine Perennou"
msgstr "Marc-Antoine Perennou"

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:17
msgid ""
"GPaste is a clipboard managing system allowing you to track and manage your "
"clipboard history in a highly customizable way."
msgstr ""

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:20
msgid ""
"GPaste provides you with a graphical tool allowing you to manage everything "
"easily."
msgstr ""

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:27
msgid "The main UI"
msgstr "L'interfàcia principala"

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:31
#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:35
#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:39
#, fuzzy
msgid "The settings UI"
msgstr "L'interfàcia principala"

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:51
msgid "This is a major release. Changes:"
msgstr ""

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:53
msgid ""
"Encrypt the history at rest with an optional encrypted file backend and a "
"storage migration dialog"
msgstr ""

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:54
msgid ""
"Add SQLite storage backends (plain and encrypted) that store the history in "
"a per-history database"
msgstr ""

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:55
msgid ""
"Migrate the history between storage backends on demand from the preferences "
"or gpaste-client"
msgstr ""

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:56
msgid ""
"Optionally run the daemon inside the GNOME Shell extension with a mutter-"
"backed clipboard provider (experimental)"
msgstr ""

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:57
msgid "Add a merge mode to combine several history items"
msgstr ""

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:58
msgid ""
"Rewrite the GNOME Shell extension history as a scrollable, lazily-loaded list"
msgstr ""

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:59
msgid ""
"Lazily load history on scroll in the graphical tool, dropping the max-"
"displayed limit"
msgstr ""

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:60
msgid "Enlarge image previews on hover via a custom tooltip"
msgstr ""

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:61
msgid "Publish copied colours as text on the clipboard as well"
msgstr ""

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:62
msgid "Capture keyboard shortcuts in the preferences instead of typing them"
msgstr ""

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:63
msgid "Raise the default retention, element and memory limits"
msgstr ""

#: data/metainfo/org.gnome.GPaste.Ui.metainfo.xml.in:64
msgid "Drop the internal X11 keybinder and the GNOME Shell keybinding client"
msgstr ""

